WEBVTT


00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:44.710
<i>Ever since I was a young girl...</i>


00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:48.778
<i>... you'd find me up in my room</i>
<i>dancing in front of the mirror.</i>


00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:52.419
<i>Carly and her street dance crew,</i>
<i>smashing it on some stage...</i>


00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.046
<i>the crowd going wild.</i>


00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.887
<i>It kept me going after</i>
<i>I left home.</i>


00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:02.959
<i>I came to London where</i>
<i>street dance led me to my new family.</i>


00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.023
<i>My crew.</i>


00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:10.395
<i>I'm still dancing and dreaming</i>
<i>in front of that mirror.</i>


00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:17.271
<i>It's just now...</i>


00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.135
<i>I share my dream.</i>


00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:53.534
We're going to be late, man.


00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.772
Hello? Guys!


00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.733
We're halfway to New York.


00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:56.202
If we dance like that in the finals
who is going to beat us?


00:03:56.203 --> 00:03:57.999
<i>Final call for The Surge.</i>


00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:20.290
Guys.


00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:47.077
- Damn they're good.
- That's why they're champions, Carly.


00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:00.826
Guys? Show some class.


00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.567
- Are you going to get the drinks in, then?
- Maybe.


00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:22.683
Jay-2-0, the next UK champions!


00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:27.987
I love you.


00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:30.289
Your round, Mac!


00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:31.693
Guys!


00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:32.896
Guys!


00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:37.728
Okay, this is... this is the
hardest thing I've ever had to do.


00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.467
I'm going.


00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:45.945
- I wanted to end it on a high.
- Yeah, good one, Jay.


00:05:45.946 --> 00:05:48.848
I'm serious. I'm under a lot of
pressure right now...


00:05:48.849 --> 00:05:51.284
...at work and Uni...


00:05:51.285 --> 00:05:53.052
something's got to give,
and it's got to be this.


00:05:53.053 --> 00:05:54.487
- So, what are you saying?
- Jay?


00:05:54.488 --> 00:05:55.922
We've all got pressures, bruv...


00:05:55.923 --> 00:05:58.024
we've got a chance to be
UK champions...


00:05:58.025 --> 00:05:59.726
...go to New York and
represent our country.


00:05:59.727 --> 00:06:02.061
And I wouldn't do this
if I didn't think you could handle it.


00:06:02.062 --> 00:06:03.296
But, you can.


00:06:03.297 --> 00:06:05.298
Carly knows all the choreo,
she can take it from here.


00:06:05.299 --> 00:06:08.961
- Can't we just talk about it?
- I've made up my mind.


00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.093
It's your crew now.


00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:20.476
I'm gonna miss you guys.


00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:23.572
Come on, man.


00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.380
This is some joke, t'ing.


00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:29.279
I'm going to sort it, alright?


00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:41.726
- You're not going to change my mind.
- What's wrong, Jay?


00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:45.037
I thought you wanted to win?
Be UK Champions!


00:06:45.038 --> 00:06:46.800
Sometimes you've got
to make choices.


00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:49.236
Why didn't you tell me?
I looked like such an idiot.


00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:53.235
I need to get my head straight.
Have a bit of a time out.


00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:56.247
Well, have a week off
and come back.


00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:59.974
I mean from everything...
everyone.


00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:07.787
- I need to get rid of distractions for a bit.
- Thanks, and I'm a distraction?


00:07:08.094 --> 00:07:09.254
The biggest.


00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:15.261
- Is it because I said I love you?
- No! It's just a time out.


00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:19.264
If you take over the crew,
you won't even notice I'm gone.


00:07:20.907 --> 00:07:22.033
Okay?


00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:27.440
One jacket, with cheese.
Enjoy!


00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:32.251
- He said it was just a time out.
- Oh, cut and run, Carls.


00:07:32.252 --> 00:07:34.981
He's ditched us all five weeks
before the finals!


00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:38.655
I can take Jay's place
in the crew...


00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:41.727
...as your man.
- Yeah, right, Eddie.


00:07:41.728 --> 00:07:42.995
Keep practicing!


00:07:42.996 --> 00:07:45.930
Let's just concentrate on winning
the streetdance finals, yeah?


00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.890
Yeah, you're right...


00:07:49.869 --> 00:07:51.666
...and then he'll want me back,
won't he?


00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:55.603
Blonde and northern.
Tragic, really.


00:07:55.942 --> 00:07:58.344
Thanks, Eddie...
Let's get down to rehearsals.


00:07:58.345 --> 00:07:59.902
Offer still stands, Carly.


00:08:01.214 --> 00:08:03.850
Why me? Shouldn't you be
running the crew Shawna?


00:08:03.851 --> 00:08:06.752
- I just dance. You see the bigger picture.
- Will they listen to me?


00:08:06.753 --> 00:08:09.422
Not if you sound like that.
You've got to be kick-arse Carly, man.


00:08:09.423 --> 00:08:11.515
Come on, give me some heat...


00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:13.421
Is that all you got?


00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:24.426
Allez. Go into the centre.


00:08:28.174 --> 00:08:31.344
I don't get it.
He's lost his family, rude boy.


00:08:31.345 --> 00:08:34.802
How can we be Jay-2-0 without Jay?
It don't make no sense.


00:08:34.914 --> 00:08:38.350
- Why are they stood outside?
- Just march in and show no fear.


00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:41.578
Come on, give me some heat.
Give me some.


00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:42.518
Come on.


00:08:42.622 --> 00:08:46.058
That was lame.
Kick arse Carly, or kissarse?


00:08:46.125 --> 00:08:48.116
Come on guys let's get started.


00:08:58.137 --> 00:09:01.507
- Okay, guys, slight hitch.
- You didn't book the rehearsal space.


00:09:01.508 --> 00:09:03.276
- Was I meant to?
- Come on, Carly.


00:09:03.277 --> 00:09:04.310
You were the boss, right?


00:09:04.311 --> 00:09:06.312
If you want to lead,
Frankie, be my guest.


00:09:06.313 --> 00:09:08.405
Without Jay,
it's a waste of time.


00:09:10.616 --> 00:09:13.210
- Steph, what are you doing?
- I'm sorry.


00:09:13.853 --> 00:09:17.619
- We're supposed to be a crew.
- Don't worry. They'll be back.


00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:21.485
Guys... I... can replace them.


00:09:22.628 --> 00:09:24.797
- Come on, Eddie.
- You got to learn from the Da Boogie Man.


00:09:24.798 --> 00:09:27.027
Listen, guys,
I don't know how to do this yet.


00:09:27.199 --> 00:09:29.690
But what I do know is
we have got a heavy crew.


00:09:30.136 --> 00:09:32.338
We've got a final in September.


00:09:32.339 --> 00:09:34.674
Can't we just find somewhere to
rehearse and get on with it?


00:09:34.675 --> 00:09:36.301
Show Jay what we're made of.


00:09:55.528 --> 00:09:56.586
Fix up, man!


00:10:04.604 --> 00:10:05.662
My hair!


00:10:22.288 --> 00:10:24.323
- Oh, Shawna!
- Sorry.


00:10:24.324 --> 00:10:26.621
- Gosh, man.
- Alright, Aimee.


00:10:27.093 --> 00:10:30.221
- I think I've got hypothermia.
- You're so extra.


00:10:31.631 --> 00:10:34.967
- We're supposed to dance outside.
- Not in England.


00:10:34.968 --> 00:10:36.869
- America, maybe.
- Then, let's get there...


00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:38.962
...but we've gotta be
UK Champions first.


00:10:39.071 --> 00:10:42.308
Only if we rehearse in a studio.
Health and Safety, innit?


00:10:42.309 --> 00:10:45.471
But we need money.
Have you got any?


00:10:45.845 --> 00:10:47.369
Don't get rude, Carly.


00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:54.218
If you let us use your studio for free
we'll wear T-shirts advertising your gym.


00:10:55.721 --> 00:10:56.949
Hello?


00:11:00.059 --> 00:11:02.857
- Bill for your little party last night.
- You what?


00:11:04.063 --> 00:11:05.197
You wanna keep your job?


00:11:05.198 --> 00:11:07.400
This ain't a drop-in-centre
for you and your mates.


00:11:07.401 --> 00:11:09.960
- We only had a few Kit-kats.
- And?


00:11:10.202 --> 00:11:12.571
I need every penny
I've got for dance space.


00:11:12.572 --> 00:11:13.538
And?


00:11:14.807 --> 00:11:16.434
Well, why don't you sponsor us?


00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:19.434
Now, that is funny.


00:11:22.148 --> 00:11:25.284
Right, off your butt, twinkle toes.
Eddie's late, so...


00:11:25.285 --> 00:11:27.548
...you deliver these and I'll
think about letting your off the bill.


00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:32.887
With a smile, Carly. With a smile.


00:11:33.192 --> 00:11:34.386
That's better.


00:12:40.726 --> 00:12:43.286
- Are you the sandwich girl?
- Yeah, is it a chicken salad?


00:12:43.395 --> 00:12:45.488
- That's me.
- And one drink...


00:12:45.865 --> 00:12:47.696
That's £5.50, please.


00:12:57.143 --> 00:12:58.878
You're welcome to stay and watch,
if you like.


00:12:58.879 --> 00:13:00.243
No, you're alright.


00:13:01.213 --> 00:13:03.306
I was looking more
at your room, actually.


00:13:03.582 --> 00:13:06.949
- That doesn't say much for my dancers.
- No, they're very good.


00:13:08.087 --> 00:13:12.023
They're not really feeling it though,
are they? They look bored stiff.


00:13:14.994 --> 00:13:16.723
Why are you interested in the room?


00:13:17.363 --> 00:13:19.831
I need somewhere to rehearse
for my street dance crew.


00:13:21.834 --> 00:13:24.530
I don't suppose you rent these rooms
for a fiver, do you?


00:13:26.172 --> 00:13:28.868
- Are you any good?
- God, yeah.


00:13:29.408 --> 00:13:33.708
Got the UK finals in a few weeks.
We'd blow this lot out of the water.


00:13:33.913 --> 00:13:36.347
Okay. I'd like to see it.


00:13:36.682 --> 00:13:38.775
- Yeah, right.
- Really.


00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:44.353
Well, we're dancing in the shopping
centre tonight, if you do mean it.


00:13:44.857 --> 00:13:47.121
- Sevenish.
- If I can get away, I'll come.


00:13:47.326 --> 00:13:48.350
Really?


00:13:50.062 --> 00:13:51.393
How will I find you?


00:13:53.165 --> 00:13:54.393
Follow the crowds.


00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:14.918
You are Romeo and Juliet.
You could die for each other.


00:14:15.354 --> 00:14:18.255
Could I please get
an inkling of this.


00:15:33.265 --> 00:15:35.631
- You need a permit!
- It's our money, we've earnt it.


00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:39.397
Ain't that your Justine?


00:15:40.039 --> 00:15:43.770
You big, ugly bear...
Justine, you come here.


00:15:44.109 --> 00:15:46.478
Is this what you're coming here to do?
Shaming me like this.


00:15:46.479 --> 00:15:48.412
- Do you want to get the police involved?
- But, it's ours.


00:15:49.548 --> 00:15:51.846
- Cool it, Carls!
- Thanks!


00:15:57.056 --> 00:16:00.321
- Everyone in Topshop's watching us.
- So, why didn't you help me?


00:16:00.426 --> 00:16:03.429
No, you know what? I don't want to
be a part of this anymore.


00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:06.296
- Don't you dare flake out, Aimee.
- Flake out of what?


00:16:06.432 --> 00:16:10.198
We're going nowhere with you.
Without Jay, this crew's got no chance.


00:16:10.269 --> 00:16:12.567
Oh, thanks. Thanks a lot.


00:16:12.671 --> 00:16:14.807
You whinge better than
you dance, anyway.


00:16:14.808 --> 00:16:19.244
Come on, out! It's all done.
Finished! On your bikes.


00:16:19.478 --> 00:16:21.446
On your way. Get your hair done.


00:16:35.961 --> 00:16:38.731
You might want to refine some of
those management skills of yours.


00:16:38.732 --> 00:16:40.028
Oh, piss off!


00:16:40.599 --> 00:16:42.726
Well, whilst you're
in this mood, I will.


00:17:12.331 --> 00:17:13.195
Come on.


00:17:18.871 --> 00:17:22.204
A little chaotic... but good.
Vibrant.


00:17:22.841 --> 00:17:25.036
Come and see me tomorrow
with the rest of your group...


00:17:25.244 --> 00:17:26.302
when you find them.


00:17:33.252 --> 00:17:34.719
Studio Three, four o'clock.


00:17:39.491 --> 00:17:41.160
<i>- Hello?</i>
- Hi...


00:17:41.161 --> 00:17:42.861
<i>You shameful girl.</i>


00:17:42.862 --> 00:17:45.591
<i>My Justine not dance</i>
<i>with you again.</i>


00:17:51.937 --> 00:17:53.700
And then there were two...


00:17:54.206 --> 00:17:55.833
I've messed up, haven't I?


00:17:59.978 --> 00:18:03.849
Changement, changement,
en force.


00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:07.683
Open les bras.
Epaulemnt Allez.


00:18:08.821 --> 00:18:11.449
Spot, spot, spot, spot.


00:18:13.592 --> 00:18:15.651
Well, would we pay to see
this year's crop?


00:18:19.231 --> 00:18:22.860
On present showing none shall
get through the Royal Ballet auditions.


00:18:23.569 --> 00:18:25.671
Well, that's not going to dazzle
our benefactors, is it?


00:18:25.672 --> 00:18:26.972
What's happened?


00:18:26.973 --> 00:18:29.141
More and more I wonder
about our methods.


00:18:29.142 --> 00:18:30.870
We drill the passion out of them.


00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:34.739
The vital ingredient.
But, I have a plan to drill it back in.


00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:36.472
It had better work, Helena.


00:18:36.849 --> 00:18:38.817
Funding cuts mean other cuts,
you know?


00:18:40.152 --> 00:18:42.484
Today it's all no good.


00:18:45.224 --> 00:18:46.452
Carly, Shawna!


00:18:46.792 --> 00:18:48.692
Oh, my God, it's you guys!


00:18:54.433 --> 00:18:56.526
Oh, excuse me... no, thank you.


00:18:56.602 --> 00:18:57.500
Mac!


00:19:40.379 --> 00:19:44.281
- You pulled it off, Carly, man.
- Yeah, this place is nice.


00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:45.642
Sick, man!


00:19:48.921 --> 00:19:51.287
- Can I help you?
- Look at this bronx arse joke, brer.


00:19:56.628 --> 00:19:58.493
We were told to be here
by this lady.


00:20:01.867 --> 00:20:02.959
It's Helena.


00:20:06.471 --> 00:20:10.305
- Have you come to watch us?
- Other way round, more like.


00:20:11.176 --> 00:20:14.543
Get this one.
'Have I come to watch them'.


00:20:15.314 --> 00:20:16.679
Not in those tights.


00:21:50.676 --> 00:21:51.977
- Crap!
- Oh, man!


00:21:51.978 --> 00:21:55.242
I'm okay. I'm okay.
I just need to lie here a bit.


00:21:57.182 --> 00:21:59.946
Oh, my God. I'm so sorry.
We'll pay for the damage.


00:22:01.086 --> 00:22:04.487
I see you've made yourself at home,
but you're in the wrong room.


00:22:05.123 --> 00:22:06.112
Hurry up, girls.


00:22:10.796 --> 00:22:13.560
- Would this suit your needs?
- Are you kidding?


00:22:13.865 --> 00:22:17.426
- This is amazing.
- And you've met my dancers?


00:22:18.136 --> 00:22:20.839
- Kind of.
- Gabe, Isabella, Bex...


00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:22.670
...Chloe and Tomas.


00:22:23.308 --> 00:22:24.832
I have a proposition for you.


00:22:25.143 --> 00:22:29.715
Unlimited access to rehearse here
for your competition.


00:22:29.716 --> 00:22:30.579
Nice...


00:22:31.683 --> 00:22:34.083
If you include my dancers
in your routine.


00:22:34.186 --> 00:22:35.175
What?


00:22:36.188 --> 00:22:39.024
- No way, we're a street dance crew, it's...
- No, say, no.


00:22:39.025 --> 00:22:41.618
It's like a family,
we can't just take on new people.


00:22:42.327 --> 00:22:43.760
Say something to her!


00:22:44.096 --> 00:22:46.832
- Helena, with all due respect...
- Thank you, Tomas.


00:22:46.833 --> 00:22:49.167
I decide the content
for your final master class.


00:22:49.168 --> 00:22:51.260
Sorry, Miss, this sounds crazy.


00:22:51.570 --> 00:22:53.972
- I'm sorry, I don't know your name.
- Carly.


00:22:53.973 --> 00:22:56.641
Carly, if you don't take my dancers,
I'll have to charge you


00:22:56.642 --> 00:22:59.508
for the hire of the studio and,
of course, for damages.


00:23:00.345 --> 00:23:01.713
It's your decision.


00:23:01.714 --> 00:23:03.515
Where are we going to
get the money from, man?


00:23:03.516 --> 00:23:06.973
- We can't win the finals with them!
- I say we do a runner.


00:23:07.085 --> 00:23:10.020
Guys, are you blind?
Bendy chicks, come on.


00:23:10.555 --> 00:23:13.752
- Can they street dance?
- No, you'll have to teach them.


00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:16.828
I'm sorry, her teach us?


00:23:16.829 --> 00:23:17.795
Yeah.


00:23:19.398 --> 00:23:21.593
This is a unique opportunity.


00:23:21.967 --> 00:23:25.494
I hope you'll all embrace it and
perform well for the competition.


00:23:30.308 --> 00:23:33.745
- I'm getting my dad to call the Board.
- Look at the state of them.


00:23:33.746 --> 00:23:34.837
Like clowns.


00:23:40.385 --> 00:23:42.819
Let's just have a go.
They'll be crap.


00:23:42.954 --> 00:23:46.219
Then we can have the studio, anyway,
and we can get the others back.


00:23:48.927 --> 00:23:50.360
Bruv, it's all green.


00:23:50.662 --> 00:23:52.152
Where's the real food, man?


00:23:55.400 --> 00:23:58.563
How's learning with those clowns
going to get us into the Royal Ballet?


00:23:59.237 --> 00:24:01.569
Helena's known for
her unconventional methods.


00:24:02.107 --> 00:24:03.506
We've just got to trust her.


00:24:04.009 --> 00:24:05.442
What is street dance?


00:24:06.445 --> 00:24:08.913
Oh, don't be a bun head
all your life, Bex.


00:24:52.624 --> 00:24:54.683
<i>Hey, this is Jay,</i>
<i>you know what to do.</i>


00:24:55.894 --> 00:24:58.727
Hi, Jay. It's me Carly...


00:25:01.867 --> 00:25:04.358
...give me a ring back
when you can, please.


00:25:05.303 --> 00:25:09.034
If you want, or...
if you can, whatever...


00:25:16.581 --> 00:25:19.141
Did I say it's me?
It's Carly.


00:26:01.560 --> 00:26:03.289
Focus, focus!


00:26:04.896 --> 00:26:06.261
Plus fort, plus fort!


00:26:27.485 --> 00:26:28.952
Right, it's your turn.


00:26:29.254 --> 00:26:31.916
We've got five weeks and
that's what we need you to do.


00:26:32.123 --> 00:26:35.251
Yeah, do we have to be so... angry?


00:26:35.961 --> 00:26:37.861
That's just the way it is,
ballet boy.


00:26:41.733 --> 00:26:44.031
- What are they?
- My feet?


00:26:44.202 --> 00:26:46.363
That's not suitable.
Where are your trainers?


00:26:46.504 --> 00:26:48.406
You know that trainers are
rule number one.


00:26:48.407 --> 00:26:51.209
This is what we dance in.
Do you want us to injure ourselves?


00:26:51.210 --> 00:26:53.268
Surprised you don't do that
in your tights, mate.


00:26:57.816 --> 00:26:58.942
Do I pass?


00:27:00.185 --> 00:27:01.914
Just trainers tomorrow, yeah?


00:27:03.922 --> 00:27:06.491
Tap, one, tap, one... and again,


00:27:06.492 --> 00:27:09.187
...five, six, seven, eight.


00:27:09.694 --> 00:27:12.754
Tap one, tap one, tap one.


00:27:13.431 --> 00:27:16.025
Let's try it to the music and
follow us if you lose the steps.


00:27:16.167 --> 00:27:19.671
- What steps?
- Has she even heard of words?


00:27:19.672 --> 00:27:22.273
All those girls are going to need
some hands on help from the Mac Daddy.


00:27:22.274 --> 00:27:25.310
Can't you just calm yourself.
Look at them. They might snap, man.


00:27:25.311 --> 00:27:27.801
Five, six, seven, eight...


00:27:29.681 --> 00:27:33.447
Come on! You're going to be up against the
best street dancers in the UK in a few weeks...


00:27:33.551 --> 00:27:36.520
Five, six, seven, eight...


00:27:40.558 --> 00:27:42.458
You're going to make us
look like jokers!


00:27:45.897 --> 00:27:47.728
Not good enough. Focus, please.


00:27:47.866 --> 00:27:50.835
Five, six, seven, eight...


00:28:02.580 --> 00:28:03.547
Carly!


00:28:04.082 --> 00:28:06.141
- What did you say to her?
- I didn't say anything...


00:28:06.251 --> 00:28:08.253
- You lot are bad, man.
- This is your fault, you know?


00:28:08.254 --> 00:28:09.880
- Ours?
- Yeah.


00:28:12.590 --> 00:28:14.922
- Carly.
- I can't do it.


00:28:15.527 --> 00:28:17.927
- How was rehearsal?
- We're too different.


00:28:18.296 --> 00:28:19.490
I can't do it.


00:28:21.099 --> 00:28:23.601
- Can't or won't?
- Listen, I'm not a teacher, Miss...


00:28:23.602 --> 00:28:26.195
Listen, I'm not a teacher, Miss, and I
think you've got the wrong idea about me.


00:28:26.671 --> 00:28:29.435
Then that will be £ 250
for the hole in the wall.


00:28:30.041 --> 00:28:33.278
Come on, I'm trying to tell you
this crew is going to fail.


00:28:33.279 --> 00:28:35.547
Because you think it will,
or because you want it to?


00:28:35.548 --> 00:28:39.074
Will you stop answering me with
questions. I don't want to lead this thing.


00:28:39.150 --> 00:28:41.380
They're never going to
get it by the 27th!


00:28:43.888 --> 00:28:46.220
Then I'll see you again
when you deliver my lunch.


00:28:48.193 --> 00:28:50.593
But, go easy on
the mayonnaise next time.


00:30:31.863 --> 00:30:33.164
I feel like a chav.


00:30:33.165 --> 00:30:35.598
These things wreak havoc
on one's lines.


00:30:36.100 --> 00:30:38.660
- I feel more comfy.
- Hey, guys.


00:30:39.270 --> 00:30:40.405
More of them!


00:30:40.406 --> 00:30:43.738
- Steph, Frankie!
- You're not doing the finals without us.


00:30:44.809 --> 00:30:47.039
- Shawna, tell them what's going on.
- What's going on, B?


00:30:47.145 --> 00:30:50.342
We got off on the wrong foot yesterday.
So, let's start again.


00:30:50.481 --> 00:30:52.745
Street dance for beginners.


00:30:53.351 --> 00:30:55.649
Spread out.
Just move like you are in a club.


00:30:57.288 --> 00:30:59.457
This should swing it
for the Royal Ballet...


00:30:59.458 --> 00:31:01.322
Just slouch a bit.
Do your own thing.


00:31:01.426 --> 00:31:04.918
- We don't do slouching, darling.
- So, improvise.


00:31:05.063 --> 00:31:07.122
You know that's
how street dance started.


00:31:07.398 --> 00:31:10.492
In the streets, in the clubs.
Ripping up the rules.


00:31:10.702 --> 00:31:12.465
We're going to break it down
for you...


00:31:12.570 --> 00:31:14.629
Like Brook... locking...


00:31:33.691 --> 00:31:35.386
Mac... popping...


00:31:45.403 --> 00:31:47.200
Steph... breaking...


00:31:57.081 --> 00:31:58.048
Come on, Boogie.


00:32:10.828 --> 00:32:12.159
Steph, show them your house.


00:32:32.083 --> 00:32:33.550
Frankie, new style.


00:32:41.926 --> 00:32:43.723
Come on, Shawna. New style.


00:32:58.743 --> 00:33:01.143
Finally, Mac. Krumping.


00:33:19.630 --> 00:33:22.326
Come on. Pick a move
and get practicing.


00:33:25.036 --> 00:33:26.970
Young man, what are you doing?


00:33:27.605 --> 00:33:28.765
Delivering.


00:33:29.574 --> 00:33:33.476
Helene, can you please
control your street people?


00:33:33.711 --> 00:33:35.880
Dancers, Madame. Dancers.


00:33:35.881 --> 00:33:37.848
That is a matter of opinion.


00:33:42.754 --> 00:33:46.349
- Chicken salad?
- Thank you, Eddie. How's it going?


00:33:47.492 --> 00:33:48.686
It's painful, Miss.


00:33:58.136 --> 00:34:01.272
You know it might make life easier
if you let me run the classes with you.


00:34:01.273 --> 00:34:03.240
Are you trying to tell me
how to do this?


00:34:03.608 --> 00:34:05.576
Well, you could do
with the help, couldn't you?


00:34:06.010 --> 00:34:09.138
We're doing a street dance...
not a ballet.


00:34:11.249 --> 00:34:12.876
So much for ripping up the rules.


00:34:16.888 --> 00:34:19.721
- He loves himself.
- Just your type.


00:34:20.491 --> 00:34:23.790
- What? It's one way of forgetting Jay.
- I don't want to forget him.


00:34:23.895 --> 00:34:26.921
Well, I think the
ballet boys are buff.


00:34:29.100 --> 00:34:30.499
We're the teachers.


00:34:31.536 --> 00:34:33.527
I'm getting my parents to
call Mr. Harding.


00:34:33.638 --> 00:34:36.630
I mean, they're not paying
for disco dancing.


00:34:38.876 --> 00:34:42.334
- Dairy's deathly, you know?
- It's alright. It's okay.


00:34:42.547 --> 00:34:44.174
Survival has arrived.


00:34:45.383 --> 00:34:47.874
- That's my lunch.
- Don't make me laugh.


00:34:49.320 --> 00:34:51.345
Look, they can't dance our way
without the proper fuel.


00:34:52.156 --> 00:34:55.683
Can't dance? Did you just say
that we can't dance?


00:34:55.993 --> 00:34:58.962
That ain't dancing.
That's just flapping about.


00:34:59.063 --> 00:35:01.531
Well, at least I don't look like
I'm having a seizure.


00:35:02.667 --> 00:35:04.635
Whatever you say, tutu tits.


00:35:09.841 --> 00:35:11.035
Tutu what?


00:35:13.644 --> 00:35:14.906
You heard.


00:35:21.819 --> 00:35:22.843
Food fight!


00:35:39.704 --> 00:35:43.105
Discipline. Etiquette. Grace.


00:35:44.142 --> 00:35:48.203
A few words I'd like to remind you of.
This is not how we treat our guests.


00:35:50.148 --> 00:35:52.844
I can only assume you know what you're
doing bringing these characters in here?


00:35:53.017 --> 00:35:54.575
You should be pleased,
Mr. Harding.


00:35:54.685 --> 00:35:56.949
Our students are finally
showing some spirit.


00:35:57.655 --> 00:35:59.350
Well, I'd rather see it
in their dancing.


00:36:04.095 --> 00:36:06.928
You've got to find a way to
work together.


00:36:07.465 --> 00:36:09.092
Get out of here.
Have some fun.


00:36:09.233 --> 00:36:10.757
Get to know each other.


00:36:11.536 --> 00:36:13.663
After you’ve cleaned up this mess,
of course.


00:36:34.125 --> 00:36:36.218
Let's ditch them
when the track stops.


00:36:36.561 --> 00:36:38.290
Yeah. We've made the effort.


00:36:48.406 --> 00:36:49.464
Shawna!


00:36:53.344 --> 00:36:56.040
Looks like you're stuck with us.
Come on.


00:37:13.831 --> 00:37:15.900
- Carly!
- Aaron, are you alright?


00:37:15.901 --> 00:37:18.926
- Are you on?
- We're up next. You been cool, yeah?


00:37:19.070 --> 00:37:22.938
- I heard there was a bust up with Jay?
- No, we're just having time out.


00:37:23.441 --> 00:37:26.569
- Is this your new crew?
- It's a long story.


00:37:26.911 --> 00:37:28.779
Hang around and tell me later.
We'll get a drink or something?


00:37:28.780 --> 00:37:30.474
- I will do. Good luck.
- Right, see you later.


00:37:31.816 --> 00:37:34.341
Okay, you lot,
you've got to watch these.


00:37:34.452 --> 00:37:37.288
These were the UK Street Dance
champions two years ago.


00:37:37.289 --> 00:37:38.456
They're the best.


00:37:38.457 --> 00:37:40.057
We used to have classes with them.


00:37:40.058 --> 00:37:43.390
So this...
this is what we're aiming for.


00:37:43.561 --> 00:37:44.391
Who's Jay?


00:40:11.275 --> 00:40:14.904
- What's that mumbo jumbo you're writing?
- It's choreography for our routine.


00:40:15.012 --> 00:40:17.845
You've got steps,
formations, feelings.


00:40:18.749 --> 00:40:20.774
- What, and you're doing that?
- Yeah.


00:40:20.918 --> 00:40:22.579
You are actually doing that?


00:40:23.087 --> 00:40:25.956
I don't think making sandwiches
is my calling in life.


00:40:25.957 --> 00:40:27.355
You've got that right.


00:40:30.828 --> 00:40:32.921
Justine, concentrate!


00:40:34.698 --> 00:40:37.428
Five, six, seven, eight.


00:40:41.439 --> 00:40:42.463
Faster!


00:40:52.316 --> 00:40:53.340
Looser.


00:40:58.923 --> 00:40:59.947
Okay.


00:41:04.762 --> 00:41:06.093
Glimmers of hope, Miss.


00:41:16.974 --> 00:41:19.738
Tomas, relax a bit, please.
You're forcing it.


00:41:20.644 --> 00:41:22.441
Go back to where you started...


00:41:23.247 --> 00:41:26.876
...and try doing it not pointing your toes.
It looks a bit too pretty.


00:41:29.820 --> 00:41:32.254
One and two and three and four...


00:41:34.692 --> 00:41:36.560
Okay, I'm going to pick it up
from this section, please.


00:41:36.561 --> 00:41:40.360
Now, Isabella, I want you to try it
with more attitude.


00:41:41.432 --> 00:41:45.095
Five, six, seven,
eight and one, two...


00:41:45.903 --> 00:41:47.972
Stop there, please.
Straight away, just slouch over.


00:41:47.973 --> 00:41:49.462
Don't make it so upright.


00:41:51.542 --> 00:41:53.237
No, no, no, you're not getting it!


00:41:53.444 --> 00:41:55.810
Your arms are too flouncy and ballet.


00:41:55.946 --> 00:41:58.881
Hands upright. Tight.


00:41:59.283 --> 00:42:01.114
You should be able to do that, yeah?


00:42:08.025 --> 00:42:08.923
What did I say?


00:42:11.295 --> 00:42:14.025
Come on.
We don't have time for this.


00:42:15.533 --> 00:42:18.934
Oh, how sad.
Crying over a street dance.


00:42:19.436 --> 00:42:21.028
Oh, bite it, Chloe.


00:42:25.276 --> 00:42:29.007
- Listen, I'm sorry if I was a cow back there.
- Carly, it's not you.


00:42:29.580 --> 00:42:30.979
Do you know...


00:42:32.182 --> 00:42:36.642
all my life I've been told to stand up
straight, turn out posture, and now...


00:42:38.489 --> 00:42:40.184
Now, they tell me I look wrong.


00:42:41.859 --> 00:42:43.690
They say I've grown too tall.


00:42:44.061 --> 00:42:46.495
They won't even put me up for
the Royal Ballet auditions.


00:42:50.134 --> 00:42:51.066
Come on.


00:42:52.736 --> 00:42:55.762
I just... I don't know
where I fit in any more.


00:42:56.106 --> 00:43:00.133
Forget them, babes.
You're with us now.


00:44:19.757 --> 00:44:20.951
I feel bad.


00:44:21.358 --> 00:44:24.128
Your students really
put themselves through it.


00:44:24.129 --> 00:44:25.829
They're nothing if not hard workers.


00:44:25.830 --> 00:44:27.797
But, they really want to do ballet.


00:44:27.931 --> 00:44:30.900
Making them do something else?
I don't understand it.


00:44:31.235 --> 00:44:34.363
- Have you ever been to a ballet?
- What do you think?


00:44:34.471 --> 00:44:38.464
- Would you like to accompany me?
- I don't know. It's not really my scene.


00:44:38.609 --> 00:44:42.636
How do you know...
if you've never been?


00:44:48.919 --> 00:44:50.477
Maybe she fancies you.


00:44:50.854 --> 00:44:54.551
- Get out.
- You never know with them arty-farty types.


00:44:56.660 --> 00:44:58.287
Jay's a fool, you know that, right?


00:44:58.395 --> 00:44:59.953
He's never going to call, is he?


00:45:00.097 --> 00:45:02.565
- Nope.
- Never in a million years.


00:45:02.733 --> 00:45:03.767
Thanks.


00:45:03.768 --> 00:45:06.970
- You don't need him, anyway.
- It's all about Jay, though.


00:45:06.971 --> 00:45:08.938
Stop putting yourself through it.


00:45:09.339 --> 00:45:10.601
Tell you what...


00:45:11.341 --> 00:45:13.468
- What are you doing?
- You call him.


00:45:13.844 --> 00:45:15.946
- Have you dialled?
- It's on speaker. I want to hear.


00:45:15.947 --> 00:45:16.913
Shawna!


00:45:17.648 --> 00:45:19.980
<i>Yeah, this is Jay.</i>
<i>You know what to do.</i>


00:45:21.919 --> 00:45:23.477
Jay, it's Carly.


00:45:24.521 --> 00:45:27.257
I know it's over with me and the crew
and everything, I just wish you'd of said...


00:45:27.258 --> 00:45:30.715
Just wish you'd said,
'you're dumped, muppet'.


00:45:31.095 --> 00:45:32.830
Carly's taking us
all the way to the finals


00:45:32.831 --> 00:45:35.594
with her new ballet boyfriend...


00:45:35.699 --> 00:45:38.068
So, go suck on that
'time out', alright?


00:45:38.069 --> 00:45:39.763
You tell him, rude girl.


00:45:39.970 --> 00:45:43.167
That part of your life is now over.


00:45:44.975 --> 00:45:46.704
It's time for the next phase.


00:46:05.863 --> 00:46:08.024
- Nice to see you.
- Nice to see you, too.


00:46:08.165 --> 00:46:10.656
Are you some kind of
ballet celebrity?


00:46:11.001 --> 00:46:12.127
I used to dance.


00:46:13.103 --> 00:46:16.072
- Helena, darling.
- Oh, Michael.


00:46:17.975 --> 00:46:19.772
I'm so pleased you could make it.


00:46:20.210 --> 00:46:22.804
I wouldn't miss it for the world...
you know that.


00:46:24.448 --> 00:46:25.849
Michael, this is Carly.


00:46:25.850 --> 00:46:29.785
An exciting young choreographer
who is working with my students.


00:46:30.554 --> 00:46:33.216
And this is Michael who is
choreographing tonight's ballet.


00:46:33.357 --> 00:46:35.257
I'd love to see some of your work.


00:46:35.425 --> 00:46:37.188
Oh, we'll see if
that can be arranged.


00:46:38.262 --> 00:46:39.661
Well, enjoy the performance.


00:46:40.230 --> 00:46:41.561
You're in every scene.


00:46:49.907 --> 00:46:52.899
- He's just an old student of mine.
- Oh, yeah.


00:46:53.877 --> 00:46:55.902
What did you teach him, exactly?


00:48:08.318 --> 00:48:10.081
I got goose bumps, like.


00:48:11.555 --> 00:48:13.423
Oh, gosh...
they never even said a word.


00:48:13.424 --> 00:48:14.822
But you understood?


00:48:15.492 --> 00:48:17.960
Not everything,
but it was powerful.


00:48:18.262 --> 00:48:21.254
- I could feel what they were feeling.
- Good.


00:48:22.532 --> 00:48:25.933
- Remember that for your routine.
- But, that's ballet.


00:48:27.804 --> 00:48:31.638
Think less, 'this is ballet',
'this is street dance'...


00:48:32.542 --> 00:48:34.169
...but more, 'this is dance'.


00:48:34.678 --> 00:48:36.947
But, we're still entering
a street dance competition.


00:48:36.948 --> 00:48:39.609
I mean, it's a different world.


00:48:39.783 --> 00:48:41.182
Same world.


00:48:42.119 --> 00:48:44.314
You'll have a stage
and an audience.


00:48:44.421 --> 00:48:46.013
What do you want them to feel?


00:48:57.467 --> 00:48:59.662
- Jay.
- I got your message.


00:49:01.305 --> 00:49:02.739
It was Shawna, she's mad at you.


00:49:02.740 --> 00:49:04.541
I'm sorry I didn't call you back
the other day.


00:49:04.542 --> 00:49:06.065
You said you needed time out.


00:49:06.576 --> 00:49:09.010
- I've missed you.
- Really?


00:49:09.246 --> 00:49:10.178
Of course.


00:49:11.181 --> 00:49:13.308
Look at you, where have you been?
You look amazing.


00:49:13.884 --> 00:49:15.283
You wouldn't believe.


00:49:17.587 --> 00:49:20.488
Do you want to ask me in?
Tell me about it.


00:49:21.024 --> 00:49:21.991
Sorry.


00:49:22.926 --> 00:49:24.757
It's me who should be apologising.


00:49:29.800 --> 00:49:31.927
What will your
ballet boyfriend think?


00:49:32.970 --> 00:49:35.962
Probably pirouette you to death,
if he existed.


00:49:38.308 --> 00:49:40.037
You know I've been waiting for you.


00:49:42.179 --> 00:49:45.114
- And you're still going for the finals?
- Gonna try.


00:49:45.849 --> 00:49:47.680
Are the ballet dancers any good?


00:49:47.985 --> 00:49:49.145
Really good.


00:49:49.987 --> 00:49:52.387
Problem is trying to get them
to dance like us.


00:49:55.525 --> 00:49:59.359
- You know there's still a place for you?
- It sounds like you're managing just fine.


00:50:00.030 --> 00:50:02.089
One minute I think
we're doing good...


00:50:02.899 --> 00:50:05.697
...then I think of 'The Surge'
and we don't even come close.


00:50:06.003 --> 00:50:08.767
- Not everyone can be a winner.
- Well, thanks.


00:50:08.872 --> 00:50:11.238
But... you've got to do your best.


00:50:54.451 --> 00:50:57.113
Oi! Fred and Ginger,
there is a queue.


00:51:02.492 --> 00:51:04.187
Why now? I don't get it.


00:51:04.294 --> 00:51:06.626
He said it was a time-out
and he meant it.


00:51:08.598 --> 00:51:12.364
Besides which...
I'm a sex goddess.


00:51:12.469 --> 00:51:13.902
He couldn't stay away.


00:51:15.005 --> 00:51:17.064
Oh, yeah... forgot that.

